**Critical Issues Still Remaining:**

**Target 4 (Thrift Codec Fallback) - NOT COMPLETE:**
The thrift_data.go file at line 66 still has `if c.CodecType != Basic` which prevents Basic codec from using the fallback. The spec requires that Basic codec should ALSO be able to fallback to FastCodec/Frugal when available.

Current code (lines 66-77):
```go
if c.CodecType != Basic {
    // try fallback to frugal or fastcodec
    if typecodec.FastCodec {
        return fastMarshalData(data)
    }
    if typecodec.Frugal {
        return frugalMarshalData(data)
    }
}
```

This needs to be changed to REMOVE the `if c.CodecType != Basic` guard, so the fallback logic executes for ALL codec types including Basic:
```go
// try fallback to frugal or fastcodec (works for all codec types including Basic)
if typecodec.FastCodec {
    return fastMarshalData(data)
}
if typecodec.Frugal {
    return frugalMarshalData(data)
}
```

The same issue exists in `unmarshalThriftData` function around line 118-124. Both functions need the Basic exclusion removed.

**Target 2 (Endpoint Architecture) - Incomplete:**
The deprecated.go file is missing the required middleware, builder, and chain types per the spec:
- Missing: RecvMiddleware, SendMiddleware
- Missing: RecvMiddlewareBuilder, SendMiddlewareBuilder  
- Missing: RecvChain, SendChain

These should all reference the old streaming.Stream interface (not the new ClientStream/ServerStream).

Please fix Target 4 properly and complete the deprecated.go types before moving to Target 5.

